+# Correcting a Booked Visit Is in Scope, Cancelling Is Not
+
+**Status:** Accepted. Narrows NG-5 as recorded in [Deleting Records and Amending Booked Visits Are Deliberately Out of Scope](2026-08-08-non-goal-deletion-and-visit-amendment.md).
+
+## Context
+
+NG-5 declared changing or cancelling a booked visit out of scope, and the 2026-08-08 ADR confirmed that row as a deliberate product decision rather than a survey artifact. That ADR also set the reopening rule: a request touching the row proceeds only on an explicit owner decision recorded at intake, and never reopens the row by implication.
+
+The owner has now made that decision (2026-08-23). Staff mistype a visit's date or its description at booking time, and the sample offered no way back. The owner asked for correction and, in the same decision, held cancellation out.
+
+## Options Considered
+
+1. **Leave NG-5 whole.** Rejected: the owner has decided otherwise, and the 2026-08-08 ADR provides for exactly this path.
+2. **Drop NG-5 entirely** — allow correction and cancellation together. Rejected: cancellation is what carries the lifecycle state the original rationale objects to. Correction leaves a visit either booked or corrected; cancellation adds a third condition and the question of what a cancelled visit looks like on the owner's record.
+3. **Narrow NG-5 to cancellation alone** (chosen). Correction of the visit date and the description enters scope as `REQ-VIS-003`; the row keeps cancellation.
+
+A second decision was taken alongside: whether the owner's record gains a link to the correction form. Adding it was declined for this round, and NG-10 records the entry point as deferred to a possible follow-up request, not as an oversight in `REQ-VIS-003`.
+
+## Decision
+
+NG-5 covers cancelling a booked visit. Correcting a booked visit's visit date and description is in scope, as one in-place change to the existing visit under the same validation a booking passes. NG-4 is untouched: nothing is deleted.
+
+NG-10 keeps the correction form without a link from any page in this round. A follow-up request may narrow NG-10 the way this ADR narrows NG-5.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- The sample now demonstrates forward-only correction on all three of its records — owner, pet, and visit. The 2026-08-08 statement that a booked visit is immutable no longer holds; the rest of that ADR does.
+- A corrected visit keeps no trace of what it held before. The sample carries no history of corrections, as it carries none for owner and pet details.
+- Correction is held to the future-date rule, so a visit that has already happened cannot be corrected while keeping its date. The PRD records that consequence as an open question rather than absorbing it.
+- The capability ships unreachable from the pages. Anyone exercising it addresses the form directly until NG-10 is narrowed.
+
+## Implementation
+
+**Non-goal:** NG-5, NG-10
+
+- [PRD Non-Goals](../prd.md#non-goals) — the narrowed NG-5 row and the new NG-10 row.
+- [PRD Visits](../prd.md#visits) — `REQ-VIS-003`, the correction capability.
+- [System design, Contracts](../system-design.md#contracts) — the types realizing `REQ-VIS-003`.
